## Always

- Practice strict Red/Green TDD on behaviour changes
- Branch from clean `main`; commit on a feature branch
- Run tests after non-trivial changes
- For launches or product-led cross-functional decisions, use `/orchestrate` — the PM as cross-functional orchestrator (customer-job triage + outcomes-shaped synthesis). With Hornero currently PM-only, the fan-out resolves to a single PM lens; the orchestrator structure is preserved for re-expansion.

## Never

- Commit directly to `main`
- Skip hooks (`--no-verify`)
- Force-push without explicit ask
- Add files outside the repo conventions (see `AGENTS.md`)
- Touch `.env`, secrets, or credential files
- Run destructive git ops without confirmation

## When the user says

- **"Ship it"** — commit on the feature branch, push, open PR. Do not merge.
- **"Quick fix"** — single small change, skip the multi-role review.
- **"Plan it"** — produce a plan in `.claude/plans/`, do not implement until approved.
- **"Review this"** — invoke `product-manager-reviewer` (the only reviewer currently shipped). When non-PM reviewers are restored, this fans out to a multi-role review.

